id: pm-fkohe8
title: "GH-1207: Make advisory health checks and strict verdict authority explicit"
description: "GitHub #1207 reports top-level ok true while the storage check has ok false with warn status, and strict CLI exit 2. The closed self-indexing finding work supplies severity and failed_because but does not make the per-check boolean or strict process verdict authoritative. Define compatible SDK and CLI semantics so agents can reliably branch without inferring precedence."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",health,output-contract
created_at: "2026-09-06T05:48:07.109Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-06T13:49:09.303Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-06T13:49:08.802Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-06T13:49:08.802Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce advisory storage and strict invocation verdicts in an isolated tracker; Publish one authoritative invocation verdict with adjacent deciding reasons; Per-check booleans and severity have documented compatible semantics; SDK, CLI, summary and full projections agree for identical strictness; Preserve existing advisory versus blocking policy"
parent: pm-larv4r
resolution: "Made SDK blocking findings authoritative for health check and invocation predicates; exposed matching strictness and exit receipts in every projection, clarified action-specific strictExit contracts, and documented changed helper responsibilities."
expected_result: "SDK, CLI and repository gates share complete evidence and authoritative contracts without weakening coverage or token ceilings."
actual_result: "Final review-correction evidence: 628 files and 8502 tests pass with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero uncovered counts; complete pnpm quality:static and typecheck pass. The final packed artifact passes fresh Node and Bun SDK/CLI acceptance, including strict health parity, inherited risk, normalized dependency/file references, invalid lineage request refusal, and zero-byte tracker source refusal. Hosted CI and review of the next head remain merge prerequisites."
